1.3

The EDR fired alerts on a specific technique used by the threat actor.

What is the MITRE ID for that technique?

SecurityAlerts
| take 5

check indicator colomn

"technique":"T1003.001 - OS Credential Dumping: LSASS Memory"

"filename": "lsass.dmp"

description
EDR detected LSASS process memory dump. LSASS (Local Security Authority Subsystem Service) memory contains sensitive authentication credentials. Memory dumps of LSASS are a known credential theft technique. Verify authorization: check with IT security team for authorized forensics activity, penetration testing, or troubleshooting. If unauthorized, investigate immediately for signs of credential access tools (Mimikatz, Procdump, etc.) and lateral movement attempts.

doing some surch in AI Chat and goolble and Mitre
LSASS memory dumping is a sub-technique of T1003 (OS Credential Dumping) in the MITRE ATT&CK framework.

///T1003.001

