1.8 

To evade detection, they disabled the built-in antivirus. But not only.

What is the full path of the registry key of the service driver they also disabled?


find registry modification activity where the attacker disabled:

Built-in antivirus (likely Windows Defender)
A service driver registry key

The tables most likely to contain this:

1-ProcessEvents → commands like reg.exe, PowerShell, Set-ItemProperty
2-SecurityAlerts → detection details
3-FileCreationEvents → dropped tools/scripts
4-DeviceInfo → host details



ProcessEvents
| where process_commandline has_any (
    "DisableAntiSpyware",
    "DisableRealtimeMonitoring",
    "Windows Defender",
    "WinDefend"
)
| project timestamp, process_commandline
| order by timestamp asc
| distinct process_commandline


ProcessEvents
| where process_commandline has_any (
    "CurrentControlSet",
    "Services",
    "start= disabled",
    "Start /t REG_DWORD /d 4"
)
| project timestamp, process_commandline
| order by timestamp asc
| distinct process_commandline



ProcessEvents
| where process_commandline contains "sc.exe"
| project timestamp, process_commandline
| order by timestamp asc
| distinct process_commandline


